  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe workspace `serde_json` now has `features = [\"float_roundtrip\"]`; every crate takes it from the workspace. Before this, an off-round float like `-14.966666666666667` read back one ulp off. Stamps hash those values, so ops went Stale after every save and load (#156 widened the effect), and imported mesh vertices drifted too.\n\n## Pins (new `crates/app/tests/float_roundtrip.rs`)\n\n- `off_round_stock_placement_and_contour_survive_save_and_load`: the stock floats are bit-identical and the contour reads Ok\n- `imported_mesh_vertices_are_bit_identical_after_save_and_load`\n\nBoth fail without the feature (`13847987139212406511` vs `…512`; 'vertex drifted').\n\n## Readings\n\nfloat_roundtrip 2, project_roundtrip 68, stock_stamp 4, operations 117, posting 17; clippy on app is clean.\n\nChangelog: Project files round-trip every float exactly, so ops no longer read Stale after a save and load, and imported mesh vertices no longer drift by one ulp\n\nFixes #169\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
